1. The problem: 60 positions, and the score of each

    90 |                                ###
    80 |                       #       #####      ##        ###
    70 | ###                  ####    ######     ####      ######  #
    60 |#####       ##       ######  ########   ######     #########
    50 |######     ####     ###########################   ##########
    40 |#######   ######    ########################################
    30 |################# ##########################################
       +------------------------------------------------------------
                  S                      *

   S is where the first idea lands (position 10, score 45).
   * is the best answer (position 33, score 97).
   There are several hills; only one is the highest.

2. Focused mode only: small steps uphill from S

   step  position  score
      0        10     45
      1        11     54
      2        12     60

   After 2 steps both neighbours are lower, so the climb stops
   at score 60: the top of the nearest hill, not of the highest.

   Trying harder, with the same small steps:

   steps allowed   final position   final score
               3               12            60
              10               12            60
             100               12            60
            1000               12            60

   A thousand steps end where three did. Effort is not the problem;
   the step size is. Every step away from the peak goes downhill, so
   a focused climber never takes it.

3. Diffuse mode only: one look at every 7th position

   position     0   7  14  21  28  35  42  49  56
   score       63  34  54  66  58  80  80  48  70

   The best look is position 35, score 80. It has found the
   right hill, far from S, but not its top: 80, not 97.
   Wide bounces cross the table and miss the details.

4. Both, one at a time: focus, step back, focus again

   phase                          positions visited   best score
   focused from S                                 3           60
   diffuse survey                                 9           80
   focused from the best look                     3           97
   total                                         15

    90 |                                ###
    80 |                       #       #####      ##        ###
    70 | ###                  ####    ######     ####      ######  #
    60 |#####       ##       ######  ########   ######     #########
    50 |######     ####     ###########################   ##########
    40 |#######   ######    ########################################
    30 |################# ##########################################
       +------------------------------------------------------------
        d      d  S F d      d      d    * d      d      d      d

   S start, F where focus got stuck, d the diffuse looks, * the answer.
   15 looks in all reach score 97, which a thousand focused steps
   did not. The survey picks the hill; focus climbs it.

5. Every starting point, focused mode only

   stuck at position   score   starting positions   how many
                  33      97                28-38         11
                  53      87                48-57         10
                  23      80                18-27         10
                  42      80                39-42          4
                  43      80                43-47          5
                   2      78                  0-7          8
                  59      74                58-59          2
                  12      60                 8-12          5
                  13      60                13-17          5

   Focus alone finds the answer from 11 of 60 starts (18%): only when
   the first idea already landed on the right hill. Where you start
   decides where focus ends.
